{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A size cut through a JSON-escaped credential can leave private content in stored gate output and model inputs."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Dropping blank lines prevents matching a multiline credential, exposing its private lines in failure excerpts."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A gate emitting sufficiently large diagnostic lines can exhaust daemon memory and stop the factory."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Overlapping registered credentials can cause per-line redaction to expose part of a multiline credential."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The common redaction marker causes otherwise useful diagnostic fields to be withheld in their entirety."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Loading and saving a run can permanently remove meaningful terminal escape sequences from persisted instructions."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Direct consumers of the artifact endpoint receive compact JSON instead of the stored formatting, although the UI reformats it."}]}